  "headline": "Road freight business entry in the six jurisdictions that adopted the Heavy Vehicle National Law changed by −2.2 per 100 a year relative to WA and the NT, net of other industries (90% interval −5.9 to +0.9); exits by −1.5 (90% interval −3.8 to +0.8). Neither is distinguishable from zero.",
  "category_summaries": {
    "competition": "No detectable effect on entry or exit. A rise in entry of more than about 0.9 per 100 is ruled out, if road freight would otherwise have tracked WA and the NT; a fall is not.",
    "productivity": "Not measurable. Transport output per worker fell −26.2% relative to WA and the NT, far more than a freight law could plausibly cause; it most likely reflects the resources boom there. Shown for description only."
  },
